        'CORE',
        3,
        'b1010000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005'::uuid,
        5,
        'The most frequent trap in retail arithmetic occurs with promotional schemes like ''Buy x, Get y Free''. The total number of items surrendered to the customer is $$x + y$$, so the effective discount is strictly $$\frac{y}{x+y} \times 100\%$$, NOT $$\frac{y}{x} \times 100\%$$. For successive discounts $$d_1\%$$ and $$d_2\%$$, the net single discount is $$\text{Net Discount} = \left(d_1 + d_2 - \frac{d_1 d_2}{100}\right)\%$$.',
        'Dividing free items by purchased items ($$y/x$$) instead of total items delivered ($$y/(x+y)$$) in retail scheme promotions.',
        '["Buy x Get y Free: $$\\text{Discount}\\% = \\left(\\frac{y}{x + y}\\right) \\times 100\\%$$", "Successive Discounts: $$\\text{Net Discount} = \\left(d_1 + d_2 - \\frac{d_1 d_2}{100}\\right)\\%$$", "Triad Multiplier: $$\\text{SP} = \\text{MP} \\times \\left(1 - \\frac{d_1}{100}\\right)\\left(1 - \\frac{d_2}{100}\\right)$$"]',
        '{"questionStem": "A clothing store advertises a promotional sale: ''Buy 3 Shirts, Get 2 Shirts Free''. What is the effective single percentage discount offered to the customer?", "steps": ["Step 1: Determine total goods received: The customer walks out with $$3 + 2 = 5\\text{ shirts}$$.", "Step 2: Determine cost basis: If each shirt is marked at Rs. 100, the Marked Price of 5 shirts is $$5 \\times 100 = \\text{Rs. } 500$$. The customer pays only for 3 shirts ($$\\text{Rs. } 300$$), receiving a total discount of Rs. 200.", "Step 3: Calculate discount percentage: $$\\text{Discount}\\% = \\frac{200}{500} \\times 100\\% = \\frac{2}{5} \\times 100\\% = 40\\%$$. Note: dividing $$2/3$$ gives an incorrect $$66.67\\%$$."], "finalAnswer": "$$\\text{Effective Discount} = 40\\%$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Calculate Total Items", "explanation": "Total goods surrendered is purchased plus free items.", "formula": "$$N = 3 + 2 = 5\\text{ items}$$", "tip": "Denominators must include free items."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Identify Free Goods Ratio", "explanation": "Express free items as a fraction of total items received.", "formula": "$$\\text{Discount Fraction} = \\frac{2}{5}$$", "tip": "$$2/5 = 0.40$$."}, {"stepNumber": 3, "title": "Convert to Percentage", "explanation": "Multiply 2/5 by 100%.", "formula": "$$\\frac{2}{5} \\times 100\\% = 40\\%$$", "tip": "Avoid the 66.7% trap."}], "keyTakeaways": ["In ''Buy x Get y Free'', always divide $$y$$ by $$(x + y)$$.", "Successive discounts diminish in absolute magnitude because each subsequent percentage applies to a reduced base."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "What is the effective discount in a ''Buy 4, Get 1 Free'' scheme?", "options": ["$$25\\%$$", "$$20\\%$$", "$$15\\%$$", "$$10\\%$$"], "correctOptionIndex": 1, "explanation": "$$\\text{Discount}\\% = \\frac{1}{4+1} \\times 100\\% = \\frac{1}{5} \\times 100\\% = 20\\%$$. Dividing $$1/4$$ gives a false $$25\\%$$."}]}'
    ),
    (
        'b1010000-0000-0000-0000-000000000038'::uuid,
        'MATH',
