        2,
        'b1010000-0000-0000-0000-000000000009'::uuid,
        6,
        'Multi-Tenure Amount Discrepancies in Simple Interest: When an unknown principal grows to amount $$A_1$$ in $$T_1$$ years and to $$A_2$$ in $$T_2$$ years under Simple Interest, the interest accrued across the time gap $$(T_2 - T_1)$$ is strictly linear: $$\Delta I = A_2 - A_1$$. The annual interest is $$\text{Annual Interest} = \frac{A_2 - A_1}{T_2 - T_1}$$. From this, the principal is immediately retrieved by subtracting $$T_1$$ years of interest from $$A_1$$: $$P = A_1 - T_1 \times \text{Annual Interest}$$.',
        'Applying compound interest formulas when the problem states ''simple interest'', or forgetting to subtract accrued interest to recover principal before finding rate.',
        '["Annual Interest: $$I_{\\text{yr}} = \\frac{A_2 - A_1}{T_2 - T_1}$$", "Recover Principal: $$P = A_1 - (T_1 \\times I_{\\text{yr}})$$", "Determine Rate: $$R = \\left(\\frac{I_{\\text{yr}}}{P}\\right) \\times 100\\%$$"]',
        '{"questionStem": "A sum of money invested at simple interest amounts to Rs. $$756$$ in $$2\\text{ years}$$ and to Rs. $$873$$ in $$3.5\\text{ years}$$. Find the principal sum and the annual rate of interest.", "steps": ["Step 1: Calculate the time interval and interest increment: $$\\Delta T = 3.5 - 2 = 1.5\\text{ years}$$. The interest accrued during this period is $$\\Delta I = 873 - 756 = \\text{Rs. } 117$$.", "Step 2: Determine interest accrued per year: $$I_{\\text{yr}} = \\frac{117}{1.5} = \\text{Rs. } 78\\text{ per year}$$.", "Step 3: Recover the original principal $$P$$: Since $$A_2 = P + 2 \\times I_{\\text{yr}}$$, we have $$P = 756 - (2 \\times 78) = 756 - 156 = \\text{Rs. } 600$$.", "Step 4: Compute the annual interest rate $$R$$: $$R = \\frac{I_{\\text{yr}}}{P} \\times 100\\% = \\frac{78}{600} \\times 100\\% = 13\\%\\text{ per annum}$$."], "finalAnswer": "$$P = \\text{Rs. } 600, \\quad R = 13\\%\\text{ p.a.}$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Compute Difference Interval", "explanation": "Subtract the two amounts to find interest earned in 1.5 years.", "formula": "$$\\Delta I = 873 - 756 = 117$$", "tip": "Principal does not change, so difference is pure interest."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Find Annual Interest", "explanation": "Divide interest increment by elapsed time.", "formula": "$$I_{\\text{yr}} = \\frac{117}{1.5} = 78$$", "tip": "$$117 / (3/2) = 117 \\times 2/3 = 78$$."}, {"stepNumber": 3, "title": "Back-calculate Principal", "explanation": "Deduct 2 years of interest from the 2-year amount.", "formula": "$$P = 756 - 2(78) = 600$$", "tip": "Check with 3.5 years: $$600 + 3.5(78) = 600 + 273 = 873$$."}, {"stepNumber": 4, "title": "Calculate Interest Rate", "explanation": "Divide annual interest by principal and multiply by 100.", "formula": "$$R = \\frac{78}{600} \\times 100 = 13\\%$$", "tip": "$$78/6 = 13$$."}], "keyTakeaways": ["In Simple Interest, the difference between any two amounts is purely the interest accrued between those dates.", "Always determine the annual interest first before attempting to find $$P$$ or $$R$$."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "A sum amounts to Rs. 1000 in 2 years and Rs. 1200 in 4 years at simple interest. What is the principal?", "options": ["Rs. 800", "Rs. 750", "Rs. 850", "Rs. 900"], "correctOptionIndex": 0, "explanation": "Interest for 2 years $$= 1200 - 1000 = 200$$. Thus, $$P = 1000 - 200 = 800$$."}]}'
