        3,
        'b1010000-0000-0000-0000-000000000011'::uuid,
        5,
        'The Fractional Period & Semi-Annual Compounding Trap: When interest is compounded half-yearly or quarterly, both the nominal rate and the compounding periods must be converted synchronously: for half-yearly compounding, $$R'' = \frac{R}{2}$$ and $$N'' = 2N$$; for quarterly compounding, $$R'' = \frac{R}{4}$$ and $$N'' = 4N$$. For fractional years (e.g., $$2\frac{3}{5}\text{ years}$$ compounded annually), the amount is given by $$A = P\left(1 + \frac{R}{100}\right)^2 \times \left(1 + \frac{\frac{3}{5}R}{100}\right)$$, NOT by using fractional exponents.',
        'Dividing the rate by 2 but forgetting to double the number of periods, or vice versa, in semi-annual compounding problems.',
        '["Semi-Annual Transformation: $$R'' = \\frac{R}{2}, \\quad N'' = 2N$$", "Quarterly Transformation: $$R'' = \\frac{R}{4}, \\quad N'' = 4N$$", "Fractional Year Formula: $$A = P\\left(1 + \\frac{R}{100}\\right)^n \\left(1 + \\frac{\\frac{a}{b}R}{100}\\right)$$"]',
        '{"questionStem": "Calculate the compound interest on Rs. $$16,000$$ at $$20\\%\\text{ per annum}$$ for $$9\\text{ months}$$, compounded quarterly.", "steps": ["Step 1: Convert nominal parameters to quarterly frequency: Nominal rate $$R = 20\\%\\text{ p.a.}$$, so quarterly rate is $$r = \\frac{20\\%}{4} = 5\\%$$.", "Step 2: Convert duration to quarterly periods: Duration $$T = 9\\text{ months} = \\frac{9}{12}\\text{ year} = \\frac{3}{4}\\text{ year}$$. Number of quarters is $$n = \\frac{3}{4} \\times 4 = 3\\text{ quarters}$$.", "Step 3: Evaluate compound amount using multiplier: $$A = 16000 \\times \\left(1 + \\frac{5}{100}\\right)^3 = 16000 \\times \\left(\\frac{21}{20}\\right)^3$$.", "Step 4: Compute numerical value: $$A = 16000 \\times \\frac{9261}{8000} = 2 \\times 9261 = \\text{Rs. } 18,522$$.", "Step 5: Deduct principal to get CI: $$\\text{CI} = 18522 - 16000 = \\text{Rs. } 2,522$$."], "finalAnswer": "$$\\text{CI} = \\text{Rs. } 2,522$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Adjust Rate for Quarter", "explanation": "Divide annual rate by 4 quarters.", "formula": "$$r = \\frac{20}{4} = 5\\%$$", "tip": "Quarterly rate is 5%."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Determine Number of Quarters", "explanation": "9 months contains exactly 3 quarter-year periods.", "formula": "$$n = 3\\text{ periods}$$", "tip": "$$9/3 = 3$$ quarters."}, {"stepNumber": 3, "title": "Apply Multiplier Formula", "explanation": "Cube the fractional multiplier 21/20.", "formula": "$$A = 16000 \\times \\left(\\frac{21}{20}\\right)^3$$", "tip": "$$20^3 = 8000$$, neatly divides 16000 into 2."}, {"stepNumber": 4, "title": "Calculate Compound Interest", "explanation": "Subtract principal from accumulated total.", "formula": "$$\\text{CI} = 18522 - 16000 = 2522$$", "tip": "Simple interest would be $$16000 \\times 0.20 \\times 0.75 = 2400$$. CI is slightly higher."}], "keyTakeaways": ["Quarterly compounding means 4 periods per year; divide rate by 4 and multiply years by 4.", "Always memorize powers of 21: $$21^2 = 441, 21^3 = 9261$$."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "If Rs. 10000 is lent at 10% p.a. compounded half-yearly for 1 year, what is the effective annual rate?", "options": ["10%", "10.25%", "10.5%", "11%"], "correctOptionIndex": 1, "explanation": "Rate per half year is 5%. Effective rate $$= 5 + 5 + \\frac{5 \\times 5}{100} = 10.25\\%$$."}]}'
    ),
    (
        'b1010000-0000-0000-0000-000000000042'::uuid,
