        4,
        'b1010000-0000-0000-0000-000000000010'::uuid,
        4,
        'Compound Interest Mastery Reference Sheet: High-speed difference identities, effective annual percentage rates, and Pascal''s triangle ratio multipliers (3:3:1 for 3 years, 2:1 for 2 years, 4:6:4:1 for 4 years).',
        'Confusing the 2-year difference formula $$P(R/100)^2$$ with the 3-year formula which includes the factor $$(3 + R/100)$$.',
        '["2-Year CI - SI Difference: $$D_2 = P \\left(\\frac{R}{100}\\right)^2$$", "3-Year CI - SI Difference: $$D_3 = P \\left(\\frac{R}{100}\\right)^2 \\left(3 + \\frac{R}{100}\\right)$$", "Ratio of 3-Yr to 2-Yr Diff: $$\\frac{D_3}{D_2} = 3 + \\frac{R}{100}$$", "Pascal 2-Year Multiplier: $$\\text{CI}_2 = 2A + B \\quad (A = P \\cdot r, B = A \\cdot r)$$", "Pascal 3-Year Multiplier: $$\\text{CI}_3 = 3A + 3B + C \\quad (C = B \\cdot r)$$"]',
        '{"questionStem": "The difference between compound interest and simple interest on a certain sum of money for $$3\\text{ years}$$ at $$10\\%\\text{ per annum}$$ is Rs. $$155$$. Find the principal sum.", "steps": ["Step 1: Write down the 3-year difference formula: $$D_3 = P \\left(\\frac{R}{100}\\right)^2 \\left(3 + \\frac{R}{100}\\right)$$.", "Step 2: Substitute $$R = 10$$ into the bracket: $$3 + \\frac{10}{100} = 3 + 0.1 = \\frac{31}{10}$$.", "Step 3: Substitute known values: $$155 = P \\left(\\frac{10}{100}\\right)^2 \\left(\\frac{31}{10}\\right) = P \\left(\\frac{1}{100}\\right) \\left(\\frac{31}{10}\\right) = P \\times \\frac{31}{1000}$$.", "Step 4: Solve for $$P$$: $$P = \\frac{155 \\times 1000}{31} = 5 \\times 1000 = \\text{Rs. } 5,000$$."], "finalAnswer": "$$P = \\text{Rs. } 5,000$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Recall 3-Year Difference Identity", "explanation": "Use $$D_3 = P(R/100)^2 (3 + R/100)$$.", "formula": "$$D_3 = P\\left(\\frac{R}{100}\\right)^2 \\left(\\frac{300 + R}{100}\\right)$$", "tip": "For R=10%, this simplifies to $$P \\times 31/1000$$."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Equate to Known Difference", "explanation": "Set the algebraic expression equal to Rs. 155.", "formula": "$$155 = P \\times \\frac{31}{1000}$$", "tip": "$$155 / 31 = 5$$ exactly."}, {"stepNumber": 3, "title": "Compute Principal", "explanation": "Multiply 5 by 1000.", "formula": "$$P = 5000$$", "tip": "Fast mental verification: $$D_2 = 5000(0.01) = 50$$. $$D_3/D_2 = 3.1 \\implies 50 \\times 3.1 = 155$$."}], "keyTakeaways": ["The ratio $$\\frac{D_3}{D_2} = 3 + \\frac{R}{100}$$ gives the interest rate instantly in one line of mental arithmetic.", "Pascal''s triangle ratios ($$3:3:1$$) calculate CI without expanding long compound powers."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "If the difference between CI and SI on a sum for 2 years at 5% p.a. is Rs. 25, what is the principal?", "options": ["Rs. 5,000", "Rs. 10,000", "Rs. 15,000", "Rs. 20,000"], "correctOptionIndex": 1, "explanation": "$$D_2 = P(5/100)^2 = P(1/400) = 25 \\implies P = 25 \\times 400 = \\text{Rs. } 10,000$$."}]}'
