        'Time, Work and Pipes & Cisterns Complete Cheat Sheet: The definitive formula reference covering the universal chain rule ($$\frac{M_1 D_1 H_1 E_1}{W_1} = \frac{M_2 D_2 H_2 E_2}{W_2}$$), LCM unit methods, and wage distribution rules.',
        'Distributing wages in proportion to days worked rather than the fraction of actual work completed when individual worker efficiencies differ.',
        '["Universal Chain Rule: $$\\frac{M_1 D_1 H_1 E_1}{W_1} = \\frac{M_2 D_2 H_2 E_2}{W_2}$$", "Two-Worker Combined Time: $$T_{AB} = \\frac{A \\times B}{A + B}$$", "Three-Worker Combined Time: $$T_{ABC} = \\frac{ABC}{AB + BC + CA}$$", "Wage Distribution: $$\\text{Wage Ratio} = R_A : R_B : R_C \\quad (\\text{if days equal})$$", "Pipes & Cisterns Leak: $$\\frac{1}{T_{\\text{net}}} = \\frac{1}{T_{\\text{inlet}}} - \\frac{1}{T_{\\text{leak}}}$$"]',
        '{"questionStem": "$$15\\text{ men}$$ working $$8\\text{ hours/day}$$ can construct a $$120\\text{ meter}$$ wall in $$10\\text{ days}$$. How many men are required to construct a $$180\\text{ meter}$$ wall in $$6\\text{ days}$$ working $$10\\text{ hours/day}$$?", "steps": ["Step 1: Identify all variables in MDH formulation: $$M_1 = 15, D_1 = 10, H_1 = 8, W_1 = 120$$. Target parameters: $$M_2 = ?, D_2 = 6, H_2 = 10, W_2 = 180$$.", "Step 2: Apply Chain Rule: $$\\frac{M_1 D_1 H_1}{W_1} = \\frac{M_2 D_2 H_2}{W_2}$$.", "Step 3: Substitute values: $$\\frac{15 \\times 10 \\times 8}{120} = \\frac{M_2 \\times 6 \\times 10}{180}$$.", "Step 4: Simplify LHS: $$\\frac{1200}{120} = 10$$.", "Step 5: Simplify RHS: $$\\frac{60 M_2}{180} = \\frac{M_2}{3}$$.", "Step 6: Solve for $$M_2$$: $$10 = \\frac{M_2}{3} \\implies M_2 = 30\\text{ men}$$."], "finalAnswer": "$$M_2 = 30\\text{ men}$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Setup Chain Rule Equation", "explanation": "Equate work fractions: $$\\frac{M_1 D_1 H_1}{W_1} = \\frac{M_2 D_2 H_2}{W_2}$$.", "formula": "$$\\frac{15 \\times 10 \\times 8}{120} = \\frac{M_2 \\times 6 \\times 10}{180}$$", "tip": "Work always sits in the denominator."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Reduce Terms", "explanation": "1200/120 = 10 on LHS; 60/180 = 1/3 on RHS.", "formula": "$$10 = \\frac{M_2}{3}$$", "tip": "Pre-cancel factors before multiplying."}, {"stepNumber": 3, "title": "Solve for Required Men", "explanation": "Cross-multiply to isolate $$M_2$$.", "formula": "$$M_2 = 30$$", "tip": "30 men working 10 hrs for 6 days build 180m."}], "keyTakeaways": ["In the Chain Rule, work ($$W$$) is the ONLY quantity in the denominator; all effort variables ($$M, D, H, E$$) reside in the numerator.", "Wages are always shared in proportion to work done ($$\\text{Efficiency} \\times \\text{Time}$$)."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "If 5 men can complete a work in 10 days, how many days will 10 men take to complete the same work?", "options": ["5 days", "10 days", "2.5 days", "20 days"], "correctOptionIndex": 0, "explanation": "$$M_1 D_1 = M_2 D_2 \\implies 5 \\times 10 = 10 \\times D_2 \\implies D_2 = 5\\text{ days}$$."}]}'
