        3,
        'b1010000-0000-0000-0000-000000000045'::uuid,
        5,
        'The Boats and Streams Velocity Frame Trap: Moving downstream, water current aids the boat ($$V_d = u + v$$); moving upstream, water current opposes the boat ($$V_u = u - v$$). The most frequent competitive trap is confusing downstream/upstream speeds with still-water boat speed ($$u$$) and stream velocity ($$v$$). Still-water speed is $$u = \frac{V_d + V_u}{2}$$, and stream speed is $$v = \frac{V_d - V_u}{2}$$. In average speed problems, never calculate the arithmetic mean of speeds; if distance is constant, the true average speed is the harmonic mean $$\frac{2xy}{x+y}$$.',
        'Calculating average speed as $$\frac{x+y}{2}$$ when travelling equal distances at speeds $$x$$ and $$y$$, which always overestimates the actual average speed.',
        '["Downstream Speed: $$V_d = u + v$$", "Upstream Speed: $$V_u = u - v$$", "Boat Speed in Still Water: $$u = \\frac{V_d + V_u}{2}$$", "Current Speed: $$v = \\frac{V_d - V_u}{2}$$", "Harmonic Average Speed: $$S_{\\text{avg}} = \\frac{2xy}{x+y}$$"]',
        '{"questionStem": "A motorboat can travel at $$15\\text{ km/h}$$ in still water. It goes $$30\\text{ km}$$ downstream and returns to the starting point upstream in a total time of $$4\\text{ hours and } 30\\text{ minutes}$$. Find the speed of the stream.", "steps": ["Step 1: Set up time equation: Total time is $$4\\text{ h } 30\\text{ m} = 4.5\\text{ hours} = \\frac{9}{2}\\text{ hours}$$.", "Step 2: Express time in terms of stream speed $$v$$: Time downstream is $$\\frac{30}{15 + v}$$; time upstream is $$\\frac{30}{15 - v}$$.", "Step 3: Formulate equation: $$\\frac{30}{15 + v} + \\frac{30}{15 - v} = \\frac{9}{2}$$.", "Step 4: Factor out 30 and combine fractions: $$30 \\left(\\frac{15 - v + 15 + v}{(15 + v)(15 - v)}\\right) = \\frac{9}{2} \\implies 30 \\left(\\frac{30}{225 - v^2}\\right) = \\frac{9}{2}$$.", "Step 5: Solve for $$v$$: $$\\frac{900}{225 - v^2} = \\frac{9}{2} \\implies \\frac{100}{225 - v^2} = \\frac{1}{2} \\implies 225 - v^2 = 200 \\implies v^2 = 25 \\implies v = 5\\text{ km/h}$$."], "finalAnswer": "$$v = 5\\text{ km/h}$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Setup Sum of Times", "explanation": "Total time = Downstream time + Upstream time.", "formula": "$$\\frac{30}{15+v} + \\frac{30}{15-v} = 4.5$$", "tip": "Express 4.5 as 9/2."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Combine Algebraic Fractions", "explanation": "Cross multiply numerators: $$(15-v) + (15+v) = 30$$.", "formula": "$$\\frac{30 \\times 30}{225 - v^2} = \\frac{9}{2}$$", "tip": "v cancels in numerator."}, {"stepNumber": 3, "title": "Simplify and Solve", "explanation": "900 / (225 - v^2) = 9/2 => 225 - v^2 = 200.", "formula": "$$v^2 = 25 \\implies v = 5$$", "tip": "Take positive root only."}], "keyTakeaways": ["In upstream motion, boat speed MUST be strictly greater than stream speed ($$u > v$$); otherwise the boat drifts backwards.", "Equal distance journey average speed is strictly $$\\frac{2xy}{x+y}$$, never $$\\frac{x+y}{2}$$."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "A boat''s speed with current is 14 km/h and against current is 8 km/h. What is the current speed?", "options": ["3 km/h", "6 km/h", "11 km/h", "2 km/h"], "correctOptionIndex": 0, "explanation": "$$v = \\frac{V_d - V_u}{2} = \\frac{14 - 8}{2} = \\frac{6}{2} = 3\\text{ km/h}$$."}]}'
