        'b1010000-0000-0000-0000-000000000012'::uuid,
        4,
        'Time, Speed and Distance Rapid Recall Reference Sheet: The complete arsenal of shortcut formulas for meeting points, post-meeting speeds, late/early departures, and circular tracks.',
        'Using arithmetic mean for average speed when distance is constant, or confusing post-meeting time formulas.',
        '["Late & Early Distance Shortcut: $$D = \\frac{S_1 S_2}{|S_1 - S_2|} \\times \\Delta t_{\\text{hours}}$$", "Post-Meeting Speed Relation: $$\\frac{S_1}{S_2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{T_2}{T_1}}$$", "Meeting Time from Opposite Starts: $$T_{\\text{meet}} = \\frac{D}{S_1 + S_2}$$", "Circular Track First Meeting: $$T = \\frac{L}{S_1 \\pm S_2}$$", "Harmonic Average: $$S_{\\text{avg}} = \\frac{2 S_1 S_2}{S_1 + S_2}$$"]',
        '{"questionStem": "If a student walks from his house to school at $$4\\text{ km/h}$$, he arrives $$10\\text{ minutes}$$ late. If he walks at $$5\\text{ km/h}$$, he arrives $$5\\text{ minutes}$$ early. What is the distance between his house and school?", "steps": ["Step 1: Determine net time difference: Arriving 10 min late vs 5 min early means a total time spread of $$\\Delta t = 10 - (-5) = 15\\text{ minutes}$$.", "Step 2: Convert time difference to hours: $$\\Delta t = \\frac{15}{60} = \\frac{1}{4}\\text{ hour}$$.", "Step 3: Apply the Late/Early Shortcut Formula: $$D = \\frac{S_1 S_2}{|S_1 - S_2|} \\times \\Delta t$$.", "Step 4: Substitute values: $$D = \\frac{4 \\times 5}{|5 - 4|} \\times \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{20}{1} \\times \\frac{1}{4} = 5\\text{ km}$$."], "finalAnswer": "$$D = 5\\text{ km}$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Calculate Time Difference", "explanation": "Late (+) and early (-) are opposite deviations: 10 + 5 = 15 min.", "formula": "$$\\Delta t = \\frac{15}{60} = \\frac{1}{4}\\text{ hr}$$", "tip": "Opposite signs add: Late + Early."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Apply Distance Shortcut", "explanation": "Substitute speeds and time gap into $$D = \\frac{S_1 S_2}{\\Delta S} \\Delta t$$.", "formula": "$$D = \\frac{4 \\times 5}{1} \\times \\frac{1}{4} = 5$$", "tip": "Speed product divided by speed difference."}, {"stepNumber": 3, "title": "Verify Distance", "explanation": "At 4 km/h: time = 5/4 hr = 75 min. At 5 km/h: time = 1 hr = 60 min. Difference = 15 min.", "formula": "$$75 - 60 = 15\\text{ min}$$", "tip": "Matches perfectly."}], "keyTakeaways": ["When one arrival is ''late'' and the other is ''early'', their time differences ADD together.", "When both arrivals are ''late'' (or both ''early''), their time differences SUBTRACT."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "Two trains start at the same time towards each other from stations A and B. After meeting, they reach B and A in 4 hours and 9 hours respectively. What is the ratio of their speeds?", "options": ["$$2:3$$", "$$3:2$$", "$$4:9$$", "$$9:4$$"], "correctOptionIndex": 1, "explanation": "$$\\frac{S_1}{S_2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{T_2}{T_1}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}} = \\frac{3}{2}$$."}]}'
