        'b1010000-0000-0000-0000-000000000014'::uuid,
        5,
        'Sign Reversal and Square Root Comparison Traps in Banking Quadratic Comparison: In banking quantitative comparisons ($$x$$ vs $$y$$), candidates make two classic errors: (1) Forgetting to invert the signs when factoring ($$(x - 3)(x - 4) = 0 \implies x = +3, +4$$, NOT $$-3, -4$$); (2) Confusing $$x^2 = 16$$ (which yields TWO roots: $$x = +4, -4$$) with $$y = \sqrt{16}$$ (which by mathematical definition is the principal square root, yielding strictly ONE root: $$y = +4$$!). Therefore, for $$x^2 = 16$$ and $$y = \sqrt{16}$$, $$x \le y$$, NOT $$x = y$$.',
        'Believing $$\sqrt{16} = \pm 4$$. The radical symbol $$\sqrt{k}$$ strictly designates the non-negative principal square root.',
        '["Equation with Variable Squared: $$x^2 = k \\implies x = +\\sqrt{k}, -\\sqrt{k}$$", "Radical Function: $$y = \\sqrt{k} \\implies y = +\\sqrt{k} \\quad (\\text{single non-negative root})$$", "Factor Sign Flip: $$(x + p)(x + q) = 0 \\implies x = -p, -q$$", "Discriminant Roots: $$D < 0 \\implies \\text{No real roots}$$, $$D = 0 \\implies \\text{Equal real roots}$$"]',
        '{"questionStem": "Compare the quantities $$x$$ and $$y$$ given by:\nI. $$x^2 - 11x + 30 = 0$$\nII. $$y^2 - 13y + 42 = 0$$\nEstablish the relation between $$x$$ and $$y$$.", "steps": ["Step 1: Solve Equation I for $$x$$: Factor $$x^2 - 11x + 30 = 0$$: Product is $$+30$$, sum is $$-11$$. Factors are $$-5$$ and $$-6$$. Therefore, roots are $$x = +5, +6$$.", "Step 2: Solve Equation II for $$y$$: Factor $$y^2 - 13y + 42 = 0$$: Product is $$+42$$, sum is $$-13$$. Factors are $$-6$$ and $$-7$$. Therefore, roots are $$y = +6, +7$$.", "Step 3: Perform pairwise comparison matrix:\n- Compare $$x = 5$$ with $$y = 6$$ ($$x < y$$) and $$y = 7$$ ($$x < y$$).\n- Compare $$x = 6$$ with $$y = 6$$ ($$x = y$$) and $$y = 7$$ ($$x < y$$).", "Step 4: Synthesize overall inequality: In all cases, $$x$$ is either less than or equal to $$y$$. Hence, $$x \\le y$$."], "finalAnswer": "$$x \\le y$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Extract Roots of x", "explanation": "Factor (x - 5)(x - 6) = 0.", "formula": "$$x = 5, \\quad x = 6$$", "tip": "Invert sign of negative factors."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Extract Roots of y", "explanation": "Factor (y - 6)(y - 7) = 0.", "formula": "$$y = 6, \\quad y = 7$$", "tip": "Roots are +6 and +7."}, {"stepNumber": 3, "title": "Pairwise Matrix Compare", "explanation": "5 < 6, 5 < 7; 6 = 6, 6 < 7.", "formula": "$$x \\le y$$", "tip": "Single equality does not invalidate inequality."}], "keyTakeaways": ["Always invert the signs of factors: $$(x - a)(x - b) = 0 \\implies x = +a, +b$$.", "$$x^2 = 25$$ yields $$x = \\pm 5$$, but $$x = \\sqrt{25}$$ yields only $$x = 5$$."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "If x^2 = 9 and y = sqrt(9), what is the relationship between x and y?", "options": ["x = y", "x > y", "x <= y", "Relationship cannot be determined"], "correctOptionIndex": 2, "explanation": "$$x = +3, -3$$ while $$y = +3$$. For $$x=3, x=y$$; for $$x=-3, x<y$$. Hence $$x \\le y$$."}]}'
