        'b1010000-0000-0000-0000-000000000016'::uuid,
        6,
        'Angle Bisector Theorem and Apollonius'' Theorem: The interior angle bisector of a triangle divides the opposite side internally in the ratio of the adjacent sides ($$\frac{BD}{DC} = \frac{AB}{AC}$$). For medians, Apollonius'' Theorem relates side lengths to the median length ($$m_a$$): $$AB^2 + AC^2 = 2(AD^2 + BD^2)$$, where $$D$$ is the midpoint of $$BC$$.',
        'Confusing the angle bisector with the median. The angle bisector bisects the angle, NOT the opposite side, unless the triangle is isosceles.',
        '["Angle Bisector Ratio: $$\\frac{BD}{DC} = \\frac{AB}{AC}$$", "Apollonius Theorem: $$c^2 + b^2 = 2\\left(m_a^2 + \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^2\\right)$$", "Inradius Formula: $$r = \\frac{\\Delta}{s} \\quad (s = \\text{semi-perimeter})$$", "Circumradius Formula: $$R = \\frac{abc}{4\\Delta}$$"]',
        '{"questionStem": "In $$\\Delta ABC$$, $$AB = 10\\text{ cm}$$, $$AC = 14\\text{ cm}$$, and $$BC = 12\\text{ cm}$$. An angle bisector $$AD$$ is drawn from $$A$$ to meet $$BC$$ at $$D$$. Find the length of segment $$BD$$.", "steps": ["Step 1: Apply the Angle Bisector Theorem: $$\\frac{BD}{DC} = \\frac{AB}{AC}$$.", "Step 2: Substitute side lengths: $$\\frac{BD}{DC} = \\frac{10}{14} = \\frac{5}{7}$$.", "Step 3: Relate segments to total base: Segment $$BC = BD + DC = 12\\text{ cm}$$. The ratio parts total $$5 + 7 = 12\\text{ parts}$$.", "Step 4: Compute length of $$BD$$: $$BD = \\frac{5}{12} \\times BC = \\frac{5}{12} \\times 12 = 5\\text{ cm}$$."], "finalAnswer": "$$BD = 5\\text{ cm}$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "State Ratio of Sides", "explanation": "Ratio of adjacent sides AB to AC.", "formula": "$$\\frac{AB}{AC} = \\frac{10}{14} = \\frac{5}{7}$$", "tip": "Simplify fraction."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Set Base Division", "explanation": "BD and DC divide BC in ratio 5:7.", "formula": "$$BD : DC = 5 : 7$$", "tip": "Sum of ratio parts = 12."}, {"stepNumber": 3, "title": "Extract Segment Length", "explanation": "Multiply 5/12 by total length 12.", "formula": "$$BD = \\frac{5}{12} \\times 12 = 5\\text{ cm}$$", "tip": "DC is 7 cm."}], "keyTakeaways": ["Angle bisector divides the opposite side in direct proportion to the adjacent sides.", "If $$AB = AC$$, the angle bisector and median coincide."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "In triangle ABC, AB = 6, AC = 9. If AD bisects angle A, what is BD : DC?", "options": ["2:3", "3:2", "4:9", "1:1"], "correctOptionIndex": 0, "explanation": "$$BD : DC = AB : AC = 6 : 9 = 2 : 3$$."}]}'
