        4,
        'Triangle Centers and Key Geometric Formulas Cheat Sheet: Distinctive properties of the Incenter ($$I$$), Circumcenter ($$O$$), Centroid ($$G$$), and Orthocenter ($$H$$). Euler Line property: Centroid divides $$H$$ and $$O$$ in ratio $$2:1$$ ($$HG : GO = 2:1$$).',
        'Confusing the incenter angle ($$90^\circ + A/2$$) with the circumcenter angle ($$2A$$).',
        '["Incenter Angle: $$\\angle BIC = 90^\\circ + \\frac{\\angle A}{2}$$", "Circumcenter Angle: $$\\angle BOC = 2\\angle A$$", "Orthocenter Angle: $$\\angle BHC = 180^\\circ - \\angle A$$", "Centroid Coordinate: $$G = \\left(\\frac{x_1+x_2+x_3}{3}, \\frac{y_1+y_2+y_3}{3}\\right)$$", "Euler Line Relation: $$HG : GO = 2 : 1$$", "Heron Formula: $$\\Delta = \\sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)}$$"]',
        '{"questionStem": "In $$\\Delta ABC$$, $$I$$ is the incenter and $$\\angle A = 70^\\circ$$. What is the measure of $$\\angle BIC$$?", "steps": ["Step 1: Identify incenter angle identity: $$\\angle BIC = 90^\\circ + \\frac{\\angle A}{2}$$.", "Step 2: Substitute $$\\angle A = 70^\\circ$$: $$\\angle BIC = 90^\\circ + \\frac{70^\\circ}{2} = 90^\\circ + 35^\\circ = 125^\\circ$$.", "Step 3: Compare with circumcenter: If $$O$$ were circumcenter, $$\\angle BOC = 2(70^\\circ) = 140^\\circ$$."], "finalAnswer": "$$\\angle BIC = 125^\\circ$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Recall Incenter Formula", "explanation": "Incenter angle is 90 + A/2.", "formula": "$$\\angle BIC = 90^\\circ + \\frac{\\angle A}{2}$$", "tip": "Derived from sum of half-angles."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Compute Angle", "explanation": "Add 35 degrees to 90 degrees.", "formula": "$$90^\\circ + 35^\\circ = 125^\\circ$$", "tip": "Do not double angle A."}], "keyTakeaways": ["Incenter is intersection of internal angle bisectors; center of inscribed circle.", "Circumcenter is intersection of perpendicular side bisectors; center of circumscribed circle."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "If angle A is 80 degrees, what is the circumcenter angle BOC?", "options": ["130 degrees", "160 degrees", "100 degrees", "120 degrees"], "correctOptionIndex": 1, "explanation": "Circumcenter angle $$\\angle BOC = 2\\angle A = 2 \\times 80^\\circ = 160^\\circ$$."}]}'
