        4,
        'b1010000-0000-0000-0000-000000000031'::uuid,
        4,
        'Syllogism Conversion & Complementary Pairs Cheat Sheet: Universal rules for conversion of categorical propositions and the three criteria for ''Either-Or'' complementary pairs. The two valid complementary pairs: (1) ''Some'' + ''No''; (2) ''All'' + ''Some Not''. Trap alert: ''All'' + ''No'' NEVER forms an Either-Or pair!',
        'Selecting ''Either-Or'' for ''All A are B'' and ''No A is B''. Both can be simultaneously false, making ''Neither'' the correct response.',
        '["Conversion of ''All A are B'': $$\\text{Converts to ''Some B are A''}$$", "Conversion of ''No A is B'': $$\\text{Converts to ''No B is A''}$$", "Conversion of ''Some A are B'': $$\\text{Converts to ''Some B are A''}$$", "Either-Or Pair 1: $$\\text{Some } A \\text{ are } B \\quad \\lor \\quad \\text{No } A \\text{ is } B$$", "Either-Or Pair 2: $$\\text{All } A \\text{ are } B \\quad \\lor \\quad \\text{Some } A \\text{ are NOT } B$$", "Invalid Pair (NEVER Either-Or): $$\\text{All } A \\text{ are } B \\quad \\land \\quad \\text{No } A \\text{ is } B$$"]',
        '{"questionStem": "Statements:\n1. Some Chairs are Tables.\n2. Some Tables are Desks.\n\nConclusions:\nI. Some Chairs are Desks.\nII. No Chair is a Desk.", "steps": ["Step 1: Inspect individual validity: Chairs and Desks have no direct or indirect connection. Individually, neither conclusion is definitely true.", "Step 2: Check complementary pair rules:\n- Both conclusions share identical subject and predicate (Chairs and Desks).\n- One conclusion is particular positive (''Some'') and the other is universal negative (''No'').\n- Both conclusions are doubtful individually.", "Step 3: Conclude Either-Or: Since Chairs either have some overlap with Desks or have zero overlap with Desks, exactly one must be true. Therefore, ''Either Conclusion I or II follows''."], "finalAnswer": "$$\\text{Either Conclusion I or II follows}$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Check Definite Truth", "explanation": "Both conclusions are indeterminate.", "formula": "$$\\text{Indeterminate conclusions}$$", "tip": "Condition 1 of Either-Or satisfied."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Verify Elements", "explanation": "Subjects and predicates are identical.", "formula": "$$\\text{Chairs and Desks}$$", "tip": "Condition 2 satisfied."}, {"stepNumber": 3, "title": "Verify Complementary Form", "explanation": "Pair is Some + No.", "formula": "$$\\text{Some} + \\text{No} \\implies \\text{Either-Or}$$", "tip": "Condition 3 satisfied."}], "keyTakeaways": ["Three conditions for Either-Or: (1) Same subject & predicate; (2) Both conclusions doubtful individually; (3) Complementary pair (Some + No or All + Some Not).", "''All'' and ''No'' is an invalid pair for Either-Or."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "Can ''All Cats are Dogs'' and ''No Cat is Dog'' form an Either-Or pair?", "options": ["No, never", "Yes, always", "Only if both are false", "Depends on statements"], "correctOptionIndex": 0, "explanation": "No, never! ''All'' and ''No'' are contrary, not contradictory; both can be false simultaneously if ''Some Cats are Dogs and some are not''."}]}'
