        '{"questionStem": "If the word ''KING'' is coded using the exact opposite letter pairs from the alphabet, what is the resulting code word?", "steps": ["Step 1: Identify opposite for ''K'': Using mnemonic KP (Kurta Pyjama) or $$27 - 11 = 16$$ ($$P$$). Opposite is $$P$$.", "Step 2: Identify opposite for ''I'': Using mnemonic IR (Indian Railway) or $$27 - 9 = 18$$ ($$R$$). Opposite is $$R$$.", "Step 3: Identify opposite for ''N'': Using mnemonic MN (Man) or $$27 - 14 = 13$$ ($$M$$). Opposite is $$M$$.", "Step 4: Identify opposite for ''G'': Using mnemonic GT (GT Road) or $$27 - 7 = 20$$ ($$T$$). Opposite is $$T$$.", "Step 5: Assemble the complete encoded word: ''PRMT''."], "finalAnswer": "$$\\text{Code} = \\text{''PRMT''}$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Determine K Opposite", "explanation": "27 - 11 = 16 (P).", "formula": "$$K \\leftrightarrow P$$", "tip": "Mnemonic: KP."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Determine I Opposite", "explanation": "27 - 9 = 18 (R).", "formula": "$$I \\leftrightarrow R$$", "tip": "Mnemonic: IR."}, {"stepNumber": 3, "title": "Determine N Opposite", "explanation": "27 - 14 = 13 (M).", "formula": "$$N \\leftrightarrow M$$", "tip": "Mnemonic: MN."}, {"stepNumber": 4, "title": "Determine G Opposite", "explanation": "27 - 7 = 20 (T).", "formula": "$$G \\leftrightarrow T$$", "tip": "Mnemonic: GT Road."}], "keyTakeaways": ["The sum of forward and reverse positions of any letter in the English alphabet is ALWAYS 27.", "Memorizing the 13 pair mnemonics eliminates manual subtraction during high-pressure timed exams."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "What is the opposite letter for H (position 8)?", "options": ["S", "T", "R", "U"], "correctOptionIndex": 0, "explanation": "$$27 - 8 = 19$$, which is S. Mnemonic: High School (HS)."}]}'
