        'b1010000-0000-0000-0000-000000000009'::uuid,
        4,
        'Simple Interest Rapid Calculation Cheat Sheet: Essential identities and instantaneous mental-math relations for linear interest accrual. Because principal $$P$$ remains constant throughout the tenure, interest accrued per unit time is strictly invariant ($$\Delta I = \frac{P \times R}{100}$$ per year). Rapid doubling formulas: money doubles in $$\frac{100}{R}\text{ years}$$, and becomes $$n$$ times in $$\frac{(n - 1) \times 100}{R}\text{ years}$$.',
        'Confusing SI doubling time $$\frac{100}{R}$$ with the CI Rule of 72 ($$\frac{72}{R}$$).',
        '["Fundamental SI: $$I = \\frac{P \\times R \\times T}{100}$$", "Total Amount: $$A = P + I = P\\left(1 + \\frac{RT}{100}\\right)$$", "Time to become n times: $$T = \\frac{(n - 1) \\times 100}{R}$$", "Rate from Scaling: $$R = \\frac{(n - 1) \\times 100}{T}$$", "Two Amounts Difference: $$R = \\frac{A_2 - A_1}{A_1 T_2 - A_2 T_1} \\times 100\\%$$"]',
        '{"questionStem": "At what annual rate of simple interest will a principal sum double itself in $$8\\text{ years}$$?", "steps": ["Step 1: Identify interest required for doubling: When money doubles, Amount $$A = 2P$$, so Simple Interest earned is $$I = 2P - P = P$$.", "Step 2: Apply the doubling shortcut formula: $$R = \\frac{(2 - 1) \\times 100}{T} = \\frac{100}{T}$$.", "Step 3: Substitute $$T = 8\\text{ years}$$: $$R = \\frac{100}{8} = 12.5\\%\\text{ per annum}$$."], "finalAnswer": "$$R = 12.5\\%\\text{ p.a.}$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Recall Doubling Rule", "explanation": "Rate for doubling is 100 / T.", "formula": "$$R = \\frac{100}{T}$$", "tip": "Derived from I = P."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Calculate Rate", "explanation": "Divide 100 by 8.", "formula": "$$R = \\frac{100}{8} = 12.5\\%$$", "tip": "12.5% per year."}], "keyTakeaways": ["Simple interest doubles in $$100/R$$ years; triples in $$200/R$$ years.", "Interest accrued each year is constant because the base principal never changes."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "In how many years will money triple at 10% simple interest?", "options": ["20 years", "30 years", "10 years", "25 years"], "correctOptionIndex": 0, "explanation": "$$T = \\frac{(3 - 1) \\times 100}{10} = \\frac{200}{10} = 20\\text{ years}$$."}]}'
