        5,
        'Triangle Inequality and Acute/Obtuse Classification Traps: For any triangle with sides $$a, b, c$$ (where $$c$$ is the longest side), the triangle inequality theorem requires that the sum of any two sides must be STRICTLY greater than the third side ($$a + b > c$$). An equality ($$a + b = c$$) represents a degenerate collinear line segment, not a triangle! For classifying triangle types by side lengths:
