        4,
        'Direct Inequalities Master Decision Matrix Cheat Sheet: Rapid decision rules for inequality evaluation. Priority Hierarchy: Priority 1 ($$>$$ or $$<$$) strictly dominates Priority 2 ($$\ge$$ or $$\le$$) and Priority 3 ($$=$$). Path Rule: A path between two elements is valid if and only if all intermediate signs face the same direction. If opposing signs clash ($$> \dots <$$), the relationship is blocked (Indeterminate).',
