        '["Priority 1: $$>$$ and $$<$$ (Dominates all other symbols)", "Priority 2: $$\\ge$$ and $$\\le$$ (Requires all symbols to be $$\\ge$$ or $$=$$)", "Priority 3: $$=$$ (Requires every symbol along entire path to be $$=$$)", "Blocked Path: Clashing opposing symbols ($$>$$ and $$<$$) instantly invalidate definite conclusions", "Either-Or Trigger: Blocked path + elements covered with all 3 signs ($$>, <, =$$)"]',
        '{"questionStem": "Determine the highest priority conclusion from the unbroken chain: $$A \\ge B = C > D \\ge E$$. What is the definite relation between $$A$$ and $$E$$?", "steps": ["Step 1: Check path validity: Path from $$A$$ to $$E$$ contains $$\\ge, =, >, \\ge$$. All symbols face the same direction (right). Path is valid.", "Step 2: Determine dominating priority: Symbols on path include Priority 2 ($$\\ge$$), Priority 3 ($$=$$), and Priority 1 ($$>$$).", "Step 3: Apply dominance rule: The highest priority symbol present is Priority 1 ($$>$$). Therefore, the relationship between endpoints is strictly $$A > E$$."], "finalAnswer": "$$A > E$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Verify Unbroken Path", "explanation": "All symbols face in the >= and > direction.", "formula": "$$A \\ge B = C > D \\ge E$$", "tip": "No opposing signs present."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Identify Dominant Priority", "explanation": "The > symbol is Priority 1.", "formula": "$$\\text{Dominant} = >$$", "tip": "Priority 1 overrides >= and =."}, {"stepNumber": 3, "title": "Conclude Relation", "explanation": "Strict inequality connects endpoints.", "formula": "$$A > E$$", "tip": "Definite conclusion."}], "keyTakeaways": ["If Priority 1 ($$>$$) appears even once in an unblocked chain, the conclusion MUST be $$>$$; it cannot be $$\\ge$$.", "To conclude $$A = E$$, every single intermediate symbol must be $$=$$. Even a single $$\\ge$$ invalidates $$A = E$$."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "In the chain X >= Y = Z >= W, what is the definite conclusion between X and W?", "options": ["X > W", "X >= W", "X = W", "Cannot be determined"], "correctOptionIndex": 1, "explanation": "Highest priority symbol along the path is >= (Priority 2). Thus, $$X \\ge W$$ is definitely true."}]}'
