        2,
        'b1010000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019'::uuid,
        6,
        'Thin Lens Equation and Lateral Magnification: For spherical thin lenses, the fundamental relation between focal length ($$f$$), object distance ($$u$$), and image distance ($$v$$) is governed by the lens formula $$\frac{1}{f} = \frac{1}{v} - \frac{1}{u}$$. According to the Cartesian sign convention, distances measured in the direction of incident light are positive, while those opposite are negative. Lateral magnification is $$m = \frac{h_i}{h_o} = +\frac{v}{u}$$. A convex (converging) lens has positive focal length ($$f > 0$$); a concave (diverging) lens has negative focal length ($$f < 0$$).',
        'Using the mirror formula $$\frac{1}{f} = \frac{1}{v} + \frac{1}{u}$$ instead of the lens formula $$\frac{1}{f} = \frac{1}{v} - \frac{1}{u}$$, or inverting the magnification sign.',
        '["Lens Formula: $$\\frac{1}{f} = \\frac{1}{v} - \\frac{1}{u}$$", "Lens Magnification: $$m = \\frac{v}{u} = \\frac{h_i}{h_o}$$", "Convex Lens: $$f > 0$$ (converging)", "Concave Lens: $$f < 0$$ (diverging)", "Optical Power: $$P = \\frac{1}{f(\\text{m})} = \\frac{100}{f(\\text{cm})}\\text{ Diopters}$$"]',
        '{"questionStem": "An object of height $$5\\text{ cm}$$ is placed at a distance of $$30\\text{ cm}$$ in front of a convex lens of focal length $$20\\text{ cm}$$. Determine the position, nature, and height of the image formed.", "steps": ["Step 1: Assign Cartesian sign values: Object distance $$u = -30\\text{ cm}$$ (measured opposite to incident rays). Focal length of convex lens $$f = +20\\text{ cm}$$.", "Step 2: Apply Thin Lens Formula: $$\\frac{1}{f} = \\frac{1}{v} - \\frac{1}{u} \\implies \\frac{1}{v} = \\frac{1}{f} + \\frac{1}{u}$$.", "Step 3: Substitute values: $$\\frac{1}{v} = \\frac{1}{20} + \\frac{1}{-30} = \\frac{1}{20} - \\frac{1}{30} = \\frac{3 - 2}{60} = \\frac{1}{60}$$. Therefore, $$v = +60\\text{ cm}$$. The positive sign indicates a real, inverted image formed on the opposite side of the lens.", "Step 4: Compute magnification and image height: $$m = \\frac{v}{u} = \\frac{+60}{-30} = -2$$. Image height is $$h_i = m \\times h_o = -2 \\times 5 = -10\\text{ cm}$$. The image is real, inverted, and magnified two-fold."], "finalAnswer": "$$v = +60\\text{ cm}, \\quad h_i = -10\\text{ cm} \\quad (\\text{Real, Inverted, Magnified})$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Assign Sign Conventions", "explanation": "u is always negative in standard problems: u = -30 cm, f = +20 cm.", "formula": "$$u = -30\\text{ cm}, \\quad f = +20\\text{ cm}$$", "tip": "Convex lens focal length is always positive."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Calculate Image Distance", "explanation": "1/v = 1/20 - 1/30 = 1/60.", "formula": "$$v = +60\\text{ cm}$$", "tip": "Positive v confirms real image."}, {"stepNumber": 3, "title": "Compute Image Size", "explanation": "m = v / u = 60 / (-30) = -2.", "formula": "$$h_i = -2 \\times 5 = -10\\text{ cm}$$", "tip": "Negative magnification confirms inverted orientation."}], "keyTakeaways": ["In thin lenses, real images are inverted and formed on the opposite side ($$v > 0, m < 0$$).", "Virtual images are upright and formed on the same side as the object ($$v < 0, m > 0$$)."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "What is the power of a concave lens of focal length 25 cm?", "options": ["+4 D", "-4 D", "+0.04 D", "-0.04 D"], "correctOptionIndex": 1, "explanation": "Concave lens has $$f = -25\\text{ cm} = -0.25\\text{ m}$$. Power $$P = \\frac{1}{-0.25} = -4\\text{ Diopters}$$."}]}'
    ),
