        4,
        'b1010000-0000-0000-0000-000000000020'::uuid,
        4,
        'Hydrocarbons and Functional Groups IUPAC Reference Sheet: General formulas of homologous series, IUPAC suffix nomenclature, structural allotropes of carbon (diamond, graphite, fullerenes), and essential organic conversion reactions.',
        'Confusing graphite with diamond conductivity. Graphite has delocalized pi electrons ($$sp^2$$ hybridized sheets) and conducts electricity; diamond is $$sp^3$$ hybridized with zero free electrons and is an electrical insulator.',
        '["Alkanes: $$\\ce{C_n H_{2n+2}}$$ (Suffix: -ane, single bonds)", "Alkenes: $$\\ce{C_n H_{2n}}$$ (Suffix: -ene, double bond)", "Alkynes: $$\\ce{C_n H_{2n-2}}$$ (Suffix: -yne, triple bond)", "Alcohols: $$\\ce{R-OH}$$ (Suffix: -ol)", "Aldehydes: $$\\ce{R-CHO}$$ (Suffix: -al)", "Ketones: $$\\ce{R-CO-R''''}$$ (Suffix: -one)", "Carboxylic Acids: $$\\ce{R-COOH}$$ (Suffix: -oic acid)", "Esterification: $$\\ce{Acid + Alcohol <=>[H_2SO_4] Ester + Water}$$ (Sweet fruity smell)", "Saponification: $$\\ce{Ester + NaOH -> Soap + Glycerol}$$"]',
        '{"questionStem": "Identify the molecular formula and IUPAC name of an alkyne having 5 carbon atoms, and write the esterification reaction between ethanoic acid and ethanol.", "steps": ["Step 1: Determine alkyne formula for $$n=5$$: General formula is $$\\ce{C_n H_{2n-2}}$$. For $$n=5$$, $$\\ce{H} = 2(5) - 2 = 8$$. Formula is $$\\ce{C5H8}$$, named Pentyne.", "Step 2: Write Esterification reaction: Ethanoic acid ($$\\ce{CH3COOH}$$) reacts with Ethanol ($$\\ce{C2H5OH}$$) in the presence of concentrated sulfuric acid ($$\\ce{H2SO4}$$) catalyst.", "Step 3: Equation: $$\\ce{CH3COOH + C2H5OH <=>[conc. H2SO4] CH3COOC2H5 + H2O}$$. The product is Ethyl ethanoate (an ester with a characteristic sweet fruity smell)."], "finalAnswer": "$$\\ce{C5H8} \\text{ (Pentyne)}; \\quad \\ce{CH3COOH + C2H5OH -> CH3COOC2H5 + H2O}$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Apply Alkyne General Formula", "explanation": "Substitute n=5 into C_n H_{2n-2}.", "formula": "$$\\ce{C5H8} \\implies \\text{Pentyne}$$", "tip": "Alkynes have at least one triple bond."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Formulate Esterification Equation", "explanation": "Carboxylic acid + alcohol forms ester + water.", "formula": "$$\\ce{CH3COOH + C2H5OH -> CH3COOC2H5 + H2O}$$", "tip": "Conc H2SO4 acts as dehydrating agent."}], "keyTakeaways": ["Esterification produces sweet-smelling esters; alkaline hydrolysis of esters (saponification) produces soap.", "Graphite conducts electricity because each carbon atom has one delocalized electron in $$sp^2$$ sheets."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "What is the hybridisation of carbon in diamond and graphite respectively?", "options": ["sp3 and sp2", "sp2 and sp3", "sp and sp2", "sp3 and sp"], "correctOptionIndex": 0, "explanation": "Diamond carbon is $$sp^3$$ hybridized (tetrahedral); graphite carbon is $$sp^2$$ hybridized (hexagonal layers)."}]}'
    ),
