        'Cell Organelles & Cellular Machinery Reference Sheet: Definitive organelle nicknames, discovery scientists, and enzymatic roles commonly tested in competitive civil services and SSC examinations.',
        'Confusing Lysosomes (hydrolytic enzymes, ''suicide bags'') with Ribosomes (protein synthesis, non-membrane bound).',
        '["Mitochondria: ''Powerhouse of the Cell'', ATP synthesis via oxidative phosphorylation", "Lysosomes: ''Suicidal Bags of the Cell'', acidic hydrolytic enzymes (active at pH ~ 5)", "Ribosomes: ''Protein Factories'', George Palade (1953), non-membrane bound", "Golgi Apparatus: ''Packaging and Dispatching Unit'', Camillo Golgi (1898), glycosylation of proteins", "Endoplasmic Reticulum: RER (protein synthesis with ribosomes), SER (lipid and steroid synthesis)", "Nucleolus: Site of active ribosomal RNA ($$\\text{rRNA}$$) transcription", "Chloroplast: Site of photosynthesis, contains chlorophyll in thylakoids"]',
        '{"questionStem": "Match the organelle with its primary biological function:\n1. Ribosome\n2. Lysosome\n3. Smooth Endoplasmic Reticulum\n4. Mitochondria\nFunctions: (a) Cellular Respiration & ATP, (b) Lipid Synthesis, (c) Hydrolytic Digestion, (d) Protein Translation", "steps": ["Step 1: Match Ribosome: Ribosomes synthesize polypeptides by translating mRNA. Match: 1 -> (d).", "Step 2: Match Lysosome: Lysosomes contain acid hydrolases that digest cellular debris. Match: 2 -> (c).", "Step 3: Match SER: Smooth ER is the primary site of phospholipid and steroid hormone synthesis. Match: 3 -> (b).", "Step 4: Match Mitochondria: Generates ATP through the Krebs cycle and electron transport chain. Match: 4 -> (a)."], "finalAnswer": "$$1-(d), \\; 2-(c), \\; 3-(b), \\; 4-(a)$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Map Protein Synthesis", "explanation": "Ribosomes = protein translation.", "formula": "$$1 \\to (d)$$", "tip": "Palade granules."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Map Waste Digestion", "explanation": "Lysosomes = hydrolytic digestion.", "formula": "$$2 \\to (c)$$", "tip": "Suicide bags."}, {"stepNumber": 3, "title": "Map Lipid Synthesis", "explanation": "Smooth ER = lipids and steroids.", "formula": "$$3 \\to (b)$$", "tip": "Rough ER has ribosomes for proteins."}, {"stepNumber": 4, "title": "Map ATP Generation", "explanation": "Mitochondria = cellular respiration.", "formula": "$$4 \\to (a)$$", "tip": "Powerhouse."}], "keyTakeaways": ["Mitochondria and chloroplasts divide by binary fission, like bacteria.", "Smooth ER in liver cells plays a critical role in detoxification of drugs and poisons."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "Which organelle is responsible for synthesizing steroid hormones in animal cells?", "options": ["Smooth Endoplasmic Reticulum", "Rough Endoplasmic Reticulum", "Golgi Apparatus", "Lysosome"], "correctOptionIndex": 0, "explanation": "Smooth Endoplasmic Reticulum (SER) is the major site for synthesis of lipids and steroid hormones."}]}'
