        '{"questionStem": "List the three Indian banks designated by the Reserve Bank of India as Domestic Systemically Important Banks (D-SIBs) and state the regulatory implication of this status.", "steps": ["Step 1: Identify D-SIBs: The RBI designates three banks as Domestic Systemically Important Banks: (1) State Bank of India (SBI), (2) HDFC Bank, and (3) ICICI Bank.", "Step 2: Understand the regulatory implication: These institutions are categorized as ''Too Big To Fail''. Consequently, they are subjected to higher regulatory supervision and must hold an ADDITIONAL Common Equity Tier 1 (CET1) capital surcharge ranging from $$0.20\\%$$ to $$0.80\\%$$ of their RWA over and above the standard $$11.5\\%$$ requirement."], "finalAnswer": "$$\\text{SBI, HDFC Bank, ICICI Bank (Subject to additional CET1 capital surcharge)}$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Name the Three D-SIBs", "explanation": "SBI (Public), HDFC Bank and ICICI Bank (Private).", "formula": "$$\\text{D-SIBs} = \\{\\text{SBI, HDFC Bank, ICICI Bank}\\}$$", "tip": "Updated annually by the RBI."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Explain Surcharge Requirement", "explanation": "Additional CET1 required to protect the financial system.", "formula": "$$\\Delta \\text{CET1} = 0.20\\% - 0.80\\% \\text{ of RWA}$$", "tip": "Failure would destabilize the economy."}], "keyTakeaways": ["The RBI updates the D-SIB list annually based on size, interconnectedness, and lack of substitutability.", "Breaching the minimum CRAR thresholds triggers RBI''s Prompt Corrective Action (PCA) framework."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "Which of the following is NOT currently designated as a D-SIB by the RBI?", "options": ["Punjab National Bank", "State Bank of India", "HDFC Bank", "ICICI Bank"], "correctOptionIndex": 0, "explanation": "Punjab National Bank is not designated as a D-SIB. The only three D-SIBs in India are SBI, HDFC Bank, and ICICI Bank."}]}'
