        4,
        'Preamble Architecture & Philosophical Lineage Cheat Sheet: Historical origins, ideals, and philosophical borrowings embedded in the Preamble.',
        'Confusing the sources of ideals: Justice (Social, Economic, Political) was borrowed from the Russian Revolution (1917); Liberty, Equality, and Fraternity were borrowed from the French Revolution (1789).',
        '["Historical Root: ''Objectives Resolution'' moved by Jawaharlal Nehru on 13 Dec 1946 (Adopted 22 Jan 1947)", "Source of Authority: ''We, the People of India'' (Popular sovereignty)", "Nature of State: Sovereign, Socialist, Secular, Democratic, Republic", "Justice: Social, Economic, and Political (Borrowed from Russian Revolution, 1917)", "Liberty: Thought, Expression, Belief, Faith, and Worship (Borrowed from French Revolution, 1789)", "Equality: Status and of Opportunity", "Fraternity: Assuring the dignity of the individual and the unity and integrity of the Nation", "Adoption Date: 26th day of November, 1949"]',
        '{"questionStem": "Identify the historical origins of the ideals of (a) ''Justice (Social, Economic, and Political)'' and (b) ''Liberty, Equality, and Fraternity'' in the Indian Preamble.", "steps": ["Step 1: Trace Justice: The triad of Justice—Social, Economic, and Political—was inspired by the Russian Revolution of 1917, reflecting the commitment to eliminate socio-economic inequality.", "Step 2: Trace Liberty, Equality, Fraternity: The ideals of Liberty, Equality, and Fraternity were inspired by the motto of the French Revolution of 1789, embodying democratic individual freedom and national solidarity."], "finalAnswer": "$$\\text{Justice: Russian Revolution (1917); Liberty, Equality, Fraternity: French Revolution (1789)}$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Identify Russian Inspiration", "explanation": "Social, economic, political justice from 1917 Russian Revolution.", "formula": "$$\\text{Justice} \\to \\text{Russian Revolution (1917)}$$", "tip": "Focus on socialist redistribution."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Identify French Inspiration", "explanation": "Liberty, Equality, Fraternity from 1789 French Revolution.", "formula": "$$\\text{Liberty, Equality, Fraternity} \\to \\text{French Revolution (1789)}$$", "tip": "Classic revolutionary slogan."}], "keyTakeaways": ["The Preamble is based on the historic Objectives Resolution drafted by Jawaharlal Nehru.", "Popular sovereignty vests ultimate constitutional authority in the people of India."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "On which historic document was the Preamble of the Indian Constitution based?", "options": ["Objectives Resolution (1946)", "Nehru Report (1928)", "Government of India Act 1935", "August Offer (1940)"], "correctOptionIndex": 0, "explanation": "The Preamble is based on the ''Objectives Resolution'' moved by Pt. Jawaharlal Nehru on December 13, 1946."}]}'
