        '{"questionStem": "A foreign tourist visiting India is arrested and detained without being informed of the grounds of arrest, and their passport is seized without due process of law. Which Fundamental Rights can the foreign citizen claim in an Indian court?", "steps": ["Step 1: Check applicability of rights to foreigners: Recall that Articles 15, 16, 19, 29, and 30 are restricted to Indian citizens only.", "Step 2: Check available protections: Article 21 (Protection of life and personal liberty) and Article 22 (Protection against arrest and detention) are available to ALL persons, including foreign nationals.", "Step 3: Apply to scenario: The foreign citizen CAN invoke Article 21 (due process) and Article 22 (right to be informed of grounds of arrest and produced before a magistrate within 24 hours), but CANNOT invoke Article 19 freedoms (such as freedom of movement or profession across India)."], "finalAnswer": "$$\\text{Articles 21 and 22 are enforceable; Article 19 is unavailable to foreigners}$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Filter Citizen-Only Rights", "explanation": "Foreigners cannot invoke Articles 15, 16, 19, 29, 30.", "formula": "$$\\text{Excluded} = \\{15, 16, 19, 29, 30\\}$$", "tip": "Article 19 is strictly for citizens."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Identify Universal Protections", "explanation": "Articles 14, 20, 21, 22 apply to all persons.", "formula": "$$\\text{Available} = \\{21, 22\\}$$", "tip": "Life, liberty, and fair arrest apply to all."}], "keyTakeaways": ["Articles 15, 16, 19, 29, and 30 belong exclusively to Indian citizens.", "Articles 20 and 21 are sacrosanct: they cannot be suspended even during a National Emergency."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "Which Fundamental Rights cannot be suspended even during a National Emergency proclaimed under Article 352?", "options": ["Articles 20 and 21", "Articles 19 and 20", "Articles 14 and 19", "Articles 21 and 22"], "correctOptionIndex": 0, "explanation": "The 44th