        '["Right to Equality (Articles 14-18): Equality before law, abolition of untouchability (Art 17), abolition of titles (Art 18)", "Right to Freedom (Articles 19-22): 6 freedoms under Art 19, protection against conviction (Art 20), Right to Life & Liberty (Art 21), Right to Education (Art 21A, 86th Amendment 2002)", "Right against Exploitation (Articles 23-24): Prohibition of human trafficking & forced labor (Art 23), child labor ban in hazardous factories (Art 24)", "Right to Freedom of Religion (Articles 25-28): Conscience & practice (Art 25), religious affairs management (Art 26)", "Cultural & Educational Rights (Articles 29-30): Protection of minority interests (Art 29), minority educational institutions (Art 30)", "Right to Constitutional Remedies (Article 32): Prerogative writs to enforce rights"]',
        '{"questionStem": "State the current constitutional status of the ''Right to Property'' in India and name the amendment that altered its status.", "steps": ["Step 1: Identify historical status: Originally, the Right to Property was a Fundamental Right guaranteed under Article 19(1)(f) and Article 31 in Part III.", "Step 2: Identify amending legislation: The 44th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1978 (enacted by the Janata Party government under Morarji Desai) repealed Article 19(1)(f) and Article 31 from Part III.", "Step 3: State current status: It was relocated to Part XII as Article 300A, making it a legal / constitutional right, but NO LONGER a Fundamental Right. A violation cannot be remedied via Article 32 writ directly to the Supreme Court."], "finalAnswer": "$$\\text{Legal right under Article 300A (Part XII); repealed by 44th Amendment Act 1978}$$", "structuredSteps": [{"stepNumber": 1, "title": "Recall Original Provision", "explanation": "Originally Articles 19(1)(f) and 31.", "formula": "$$\\text{Part III Fundamental Right (Pre-1978)}$$", "tip": "Subject to frequent land reform litigation."}, {"stepNumber": 2, "title": "Identify Amending Act", "explanation": "44th Constitutional Amendment Act 1978.", "formula": "$$\\text{44th CAA, 1978}$$", "tip": "Removed from Part III."}, {"stepNumber": 3, "title": "State Current Location", "explanation": "Article 300A in Part XII.", "formula": "$$\\text{Article 300A} \\implies \\text{Ordinary legal right}$$", "tip": "No Article 32 direct remedy."}], "keyTakeaways": ["The Right to Property is a legal right under Article 300A, not a Fundamental Right.", "Article 21A (Right to Free and Compulsory Education for ages 6-14) was added by the 86th Constitutional Amendment Act of 2002."], "quickCheckItems": [{"question": "Which constitutional amendment added Article 21A (Right to Education) to the Indian Constitution?", "options": ["86th Amendment Act 2002", "44th Amendment Act 1978", "42nd Amendment Act 1976", "91st Amendment Act 2003"], "correctOptionIndex": 0, "explanation": "The 86th Constitutional Amendment Act of 2002 inserted Article 21A making free and compulsory education for children aged 6 to 14 a Fundamental Right."}]}'
