        'Dangling Participles & Misplaced Modifier Correction: A participial phrase positioned at the start of a sentence must logically and grammatically modify the NOUN that immediately follows the comma. When the grammatical subject following the comma is incapable of performing the participial action (e.g., ''Walking down the road, a speeding car hit him''), the participle ''dangles'' because a car cannot walk down the road! Correction methods:
