        5,
        'The Limiting Modifier Placement Trap (''Only'', ''Just'', ''Almost'', ''Hardly''): In English syntax, limiting modifiers change the semantic meaning of a sentence entirely depending on their precise placement. The word ''only'' must be placed immediately adjacent to the word it restricts:
- ''Only Sheel eats apples at noon.'' (Nobody else eats apples at noon)
- ''Sheel only eats apples at noon.'' (He does nothing else with apples but eat them)
- ''Sheel eats only apples at noon.'' (He eats nothing other than apples)
- ''Sheel eats apples only at noon.'' (He eats apples at no other time)
